      "obligation": "refuter:20:1",
      "id": "thm-pcp-theorem-np-equals-pcp-log-n-o-one",
      "location": "Proof step 2.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The dependency `def-pcp-class-with-completeness-and-soundness` permits `$0\\le s<c\\le1$` to be any constants independent of input length; it does not require `s` to be rational or computable. Step 2.1 defines the certificate relation using acceptance probability `>s` and claims a deterministic machine can compare that rational probability with `s` by integer arithmetic. For an arbitrary real `s`, this comparison need not be computable, so the step does not establish that the paired language is in P as written. Fixing a rational `s'` with `s<s'<1` and using `>s'` repairs this proof gap.",
      "severity": "nonfatal",
